 "notes": "foot = [x, y] in px from the top left of the image: where the thing touches the ground. For villagers and animals it is the point between the feet; for buildings, farms, mines and the water patches it is the centre of the footprint (the game hotspot), so the front of a building reaches below it. Put every foot on one ground line. Villagers all face game direction 1 (east, slightly toward the viewer), so the target goes on their right; the animals face direction 7 (toward the villager). Villager WebPs keep every 2nd game frame at 45 ms (quality 55, alpha 50, method 4), like the idle sprites. scale = output px per x2 game px: villagers and animals 1.4, trees smaller (~165 px tall instead of ~460), buildings 0.23 to 0.57 so they land at 140 to 180 px, small buildings (palisade, foundation) use the house scale. Buildings: Feudal Age Western European where the game has one, Castle Age for siege workshop, monastery and castle (they have no earlier look), Dark Age generic outpost and palisade; *_dark are the Dark Age generic look of house, mill, barracks, dock and town center. obj_farm is a freshly sown farm, bld_farm a grown one (both drawn from the farm ground textures, 3 x 3 tiles). Player colour is blue (42, 94, 207) like the idle sprites."
}